 the record here runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025 on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. April to May came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those years, more than any other pair, and it is also the wettest pair at 9.11 inches normal. In 2026 so far, January to February sat at 43% of normal and February to March at 154%. Grid 22977 had its driest year in 1987 at 66% of normal.</p>"}
